breaking_changes.Adaptation_method:
Remove usage of promise.isResolved(), promise.isFulfilled(), promise.isRejected(), and promise.isPending(). Redesign code to use Promise chaining, .then/.catch, or async/await for detecting completion, fulfillment, or rejection states.

Before:
promise.isFulfilled();

After:
// use .then or .catch
promise.then(() => { /* fulfilled */ }, () => { /* rejected */ });
// or async/await
try { await promise; /* fulfilled */ } catch(e) { /* rejected */ }

Replace Promise.defer() with manual new Promise construction.

Before:
var deferred = Promise.defer();
deferred.resolve(value);

deferred.promise.then(...);

After:
var deferred = {};
deferred.promise = new Promise(function(resolve, reject) {
  deferred.resolve = resolve;
  deferred.reject = reject;
});
deferred.resolve(value);
deferred.promise.then(...);

Change usage of .catch('ErrorType', handler) to .catch(handler). To filter by error type, use .catch(err => { if (err instanceof ErrorType) ... }).

Before:
promise.catch('TypeError', handler);

After:
promise.catch(err => {
  if (err instanceof TypeError) handler(err);
});

Enable long stack traces explicitly:

Before:
// long stack traces were enabled by default (in development)

After:
Promise.config({ longStackTraces: true });

Change use of second positional argument to pass an options object:

Before (2.x):
Promise.promisify(fn, ctx);

After (3.0):
Promise.promisify(fn, {context: ctx});

Remove the second argument from calls to .spread(). Migrate logic previously in the second argument to run after the spread handler, or refactor into the main handler as appropriate.

Before (2.x):
promise.spread(handler, secondArg);

After (3.0):
promise.spread(handler);
// move logic from secondArg after .spread or into handler.

Remove usage of .done(), or ensure that all promises ended with .done() have proper error handling in place.

Before:
promise.done();

After:
promise.then(...).catch(...);
